// Title: Credentials In Files
// Sigma ID: 53b1b378-9b06-4992-b972-dde6e423d2b4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Igor Fits, Mikhail Larin, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-19 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.001
// Description: Detecting attempts to extract passwords with grep and laZagne
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1552.001/T1552.001.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_find_cred_in_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/grep" and ProcessCommandLine contains "password") or ProcessCommandLine contains "laZagne"
